  "name": "Witch Hunter Smoke Grenade accelerates allies and blocks hostile targeting across its edge (#3943)",
  "contract": [
    "Smoke Grenade 805756 promises an 8-second, 8-yard cloud, 40% ally movement speed from 805757, 60% enemy slow, and enemies unable to target into or out of the smoke. The class completion hooks cast a friendly persistent aura and gate hostile targeting across the cloud. This regression exercises the complete reported mechanic through ordinary casts and opposing PvP-enabled players outside sanctuary.",
    "A Horde mage 7 yards from the cloud center and an Alliance target 10.5 yards from it are 3.5 yards apart. Their ordinary Fire Blast works before smoke. With the Horde mage inside and the victim outside, the same cast is rejected; a target 7.5 yards from the center, inside the same cloud remains attackable. The inverse outside-to-inside cast is also rejected. After expiry, the original target is attackable again. Ally speed rises from 1.0 to 1.4 and enemy speed falls to 0.4 only while the cloud is active. Fire Blast cooldown is reset between independent controls; normal cast, resource, targeting and aura rules remain enabled.",
    "The helper must be a beneficial aura on its caster and nearby allies, and must never apply to the opposing player. Its native persistent-area ally selector and aura polarity are part of the reported friendly speed mechanic."
  ],
